      ["How is the letter ಕ read on its own?",["k, with no vowel","ka, and the a is always said","kā, with a long a","ke"],1,"Every consonant letter carries an a, and Kannada always says it: ಕ is ka."],
      ["What is the difference between ಎ and ಏ?",["None: they are two ways to write one sound","ಏ is said through the nose","ಎ is short e, ಏ is long ē, and Kannada tells them apart","ಏ is used only in Sanskrit words"],2,"ಎ is short, as in bet; ಏ is long, as in say held without the glide."]
